-- EXPECT-ERROR: refinement violation
-- The stdlib contract itself, exercised across a module boundary: `List.head`
-- declares `{List(a) | len(_) > 0}`, and this call passes the empty literal.
--
-- Distinct from t114, which declares its own contract in the same module. This
-- file additionally pins that a refinement written in a STDLIB signature is
-- visible to a user program's call site — the stdlib declarations are merged
-- into the module the checker sees, and a contract nobody can see is a contract
-- that does nothing. It also pins that the panic inside `List.head` is now
-- backed by a compile-time check, not only a runtime abort.
mod T116 do

  fn main() : Int do
    List.head([])
  end

end
